ions used NEON; removing it might slow down but correctness is priority.\n\nBut wait: The current source already has NEON code inside the group loop. If we restructure to have persistent local_size, we can keep that NEON code as is, just move the parallel region structure.\n\nLet me write the corrected version:\n\n```c\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group *groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    int max_threads = omp_get_max_threads();\n    if (max_threads < 1) max_threads = 1;\n\n    HeapNode **thread_heaps = malloc(max_threads * sizeof(HeapNode*));\n    for (int t = 0; t < max_threads; t++) {\n        thread_heaps[t] = malloc((k + 1) * sizeof(HeapNode));\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n            thread_heaps[t][i].dist = FLT_MAX;\n            thread_heaps[t][i].label = -1;\n        }\n    }\n\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n        HeapNode *local_heap = thread_heaps[tid];\n        int local_size = 0;\n\n        #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n        for (int gi = 0; gi < n_groups; gi++) {\n            Group g = groups[gi];\n            float *xs = g.xs;\n            float *ys = g.ys;\n            int len = g.length;\n            char label = g.label;\n\n            // Process in batches of 4 using NEON\n            int j = 0;\n            for (; j + 3 < len; j += 4) {\n                float32x4_t x_vec = vld1q_f32(xs + j);\n                float32x4_t y_vec = vld1q_f32(ys + j);\n                float tx = to_evaluate.x;\n                float ty = to_evaluate.y;\n                float32x4_t dx = vsubq_f32(x_vec, vdupq_n_f32(tx));\n                float32x4_t dy = vsubq_f32(y_vec, vdupq_n_f32(ty));\n                float32x4_t dist_sq = vmlaq_f32(vmulq_f32(dx, dx), dy, dy);\n                float d[4];\n                vst1q_f32(d, dist_sq);\n                for (int t2 = 0; t2 < 4; t2++) {\n                    heap_insert_or_replace(d[t2], label, local_heap, &local_size, k);\n                }\n            }\n            // Scalar remainder\n            for (; j < len; j++) {\n                float dx = xs[j] - to_evaluate.x;\n                float dy = ys[j] - to_evaluate.y;\n                float d = dx*dx + dy*dy;\n                heap_insert_or_replace(d, label, local_heap, &local_size, k);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Store final size for this thread\n        #pragma omp critical\n        {\n            // Actually we can just store after loop; no need critical since each tid writes its own element.\n            // But to be safe:\n            int *sizes = (int*)malloc(max_threads*sizeof(int)); // not good\n        }\n    }\n\n    // After parallel region, thread_sizes array needed. We'll use an array allocated before parallel and updated inside.\n```\n\nBetter: allocate `thread_sizes` array of size max_threads initialized to 0. Inside parallel region, after processing all groups for that thread, store local_size into thread_sizes[tid]. Since each tid writes its own element, no race.\n\nSo:\n\n```c\nint *thread_sizes = calloc(max_threads, sizeof(int));\n#pragma omp parallel\n{\n    int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n    HeapNode *local_heap = thread_heaps[tid];\n    int local_size = 0;\n    #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n    for (int gi = 0; gi < n_groups; gi++) {\n        // ... process group, updating local_size\n    }\n    thread_sizes[tid] = local_size;\n}\n```\n\nThat works.\n\nThen merge as before.\n\nNow tie-breaking: after computing freq array:\n\n```c\nint max_freq = 0;\nfor (int c = 0; c < 256; c++) {\n    if (freq[c] > max_freq) max_freq = freq[c];\n}\nchar best_label = '?';\nfor (int c = 0; c < 255; c++) { // actually up to 255\n    if (freq[c] == max_freq) {\n        best_label = (char)c;\n        break;\n    }\n}\nreturn best_label;\n```\n\nBut note: labels can be any char, including negative values? In C, char may be signed. We cast to unsigned char when indexing freq array. So we need to iterate over all 256 possible unsigned char values. Us